<Base
  title="Privacy policy: Calquna"
  description="What Calquna does and does not collect. Short version: the calculators collect nothing, because they run in your browser."
>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="lede">Short version: the calculators collect nothing, because they run in your browser.</p>

  <h2>What happens when you use a calculator</h2>
  <p>
    Every sum on this site is worked out by a small script on the page itself. The dates,
    numbers and text you type never leave your device. There is no account, no sign-up, and no
    database of calculations. When you close the tab, what you typed is gone.
  </p>

  <h2>What the site does measure</h2>
  <p>
    Like most websites, Calquna counts visits in aggregate: which pages are read, roughly
    which country visitors come from, and whether they arrived from a search engine. This is
    used to decide which calculators to build next. It is not used to build a profile of you.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    This site is supported by advertising served by Google AdSense. Google may use cookies to
    serve ads based on your visits to this and other websites. You can turn off personalised
    advertising in your Google ad settings, and you can block or clear cookies in your browser
    at any time. The calculators work exactly the same with ads blocked.
  </p>

  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>
    If you write to us, we keep the message so we can reply and fix whatever you reported. We
    do not add you to a mailing list, because there is not one.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the new version goes on this page with a new date at the bottom.
    Page last checked 13 November 2026.
  </p>
</Base>
